"""Class 6 SST Ch 13 The Value of Work - Hard-tier extras."""
from common import AR4, Q

AR = [
 AR4("A farmer selling vegetables in the market performs an economic activity.", "Economic activities are done in exchange for money or money's worth.", "a",
     "R defines economic activity, and the farmer earns income, so R explains A."),
 AR4("A mother cooking for her family is doing a non-economic activity.", "Non-economic activities are done out of love, care and respect without expecting payment.", "a",
     "R gives the meaning of non-economic activity, which fits A."),
 AR4("A salary is a fixed payment made regularly, usually every month.", "A wage is paid to a doctor for professional advice.", "c",
     "A is true; R is false, payment for professional advice is a fee."),
 AR4("Payment in kind means payment in goods instead of money.", "A fee is the charge for professional advice or services.", "b",
     "Both are true, but they describe different types of payment, so R does not explain A."),
 AR4("Only economic activities have value for society.", "Care and household work done without pay also contribute to the well-being of families.", "d",
     "A is false, because non-economic work also has great value; R is true."),
 AR4("Wages are generally paid for a specific period of work, such as a day.", "A salary is paid to labourers only when they sell goods in a market.", "c",
     "A is true; R is false, a salary is a regular payment from an employer, not a payment for sold goods."),
]

CASE = [
 Q("<b>Case study.</b> Ramu works as a mason and is paid Rs 700 for each day he works. His wife, Sita, runs the home, cooks meals and looks after his elderly mother. His neighbour, Dr Anita, charges Rs 400 per patient at her clinic. "
   "(i) What is Ramu's payment called? (ii) What is the payment received by Dr Anita called? (iii) Is Sita's work an economic or a non-economic activity? (iv) Why should Sita's work also be respected even though she gets no pay?",
   "(i) A wage (1). (ii) A fee (1). (iii) Non-economic activity (1). (iv) She works out of love and care (1); her work keeps the family healthy and supports those who earn, so it has real value though it gets no money (1).", "1+1+1+2"),
 Q("<b>Case study.</b> In a village in Odisha, Bhola works on a farm during harvest. Instead of money, the farmer gives him 20 kg of rice for each week of work. At the same time, Bhola's brother, Gopal, works in a town office and receives Rs 25,000 on the last day of every month. "
   "(i) What type of payment does Bhola receive? (ii) Which word describes the payment Gopal receives? (iii) Which of the two receives pay in money? (iv) State one difficulty in payment in kind compared with payment in money.",
   "(i) Payment in kind (1). (ii) Salary (1). (iii) Gopal (1). (iv) Goods cannot easily be used to buy other things or divided in small amounts (1); their value may also be hard to measure or may differ (1).", "1+1+1+2"),
 Q("<b>Case study.</b> On Sundays, Arjun and his friends clean the lane in front of their houses without any payment. The municipality's sweeper, Raju, does the same work on other days and is paid for it. People respect both for keeping the area clean. "
   "(i) Whose work is non-economic here? (ii) Whose work is economic? (iii) What term means respect for all kinds of work? (iv) Why is it wrong to look down on work like sweeping?",
   "(i) Arjun and his friends (1). (ii) Raju's (1). (iii) Dignity of labour (1). (iv) All useful work serves society (1); a clean neighbourhood depends on such workers, so every honest job deserves equal respect (1).", "1+1+1+2"),
]

